    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b6315b9_04c7c1e9",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T18:38:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am tying to hash the actually lines in the file_context file. e.g.\n/data(/.*)?\t\tu:object_r:system_data_file:s0\n/data/.layout_version\t\tu:object_r:install_data_file:s0\n/data/unencrypted(/.*)?         u:object_r:unencrypted_data_file:s0\n/data/backup(/.*)?\t\tu:object_r:backup_data_file:s0\n/data/secure/backup(/.*)?\tu:object_r:backup_data_file:s0\n/data/system/ndebugsocket\tu:object_r:system_ndebug_socket:s0\n\n\nSo the regex_str and ctx_raw are directly read from the file, while other fields are intermediate attributes. Since it\u0027s more difficult to reference the actually line contents in the file, I just use \"regex_str+ctx_raw\" as the base information.",
      "parentUuid": "3e2c092b_4c33aceb",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
